pportunities for STEM professionals such as AI researchers, computer vision engineers, and data scientists.", "image": "https://imageio.forbes.com/specials-images/imageserve/6a4187fe541ff24cc1184c0c/0x0.jpg?format=jpg&height=900&width=1600&fit=bounds", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=forbes.com&sz=64"}]}}, "Other": {"expires_at": 1785197406.985651, "feed": {"family": "Other", "fetched_at": "2026-07-27T18:10:06+00:00", "items": [{"title": "Why Humanities Majors Are 2026\u2019s Stealth Power Players In Tech", "source": "Forbes", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEmDd_sXQmfYDz_BLUXjjeIUSxm65hgxutjHbqHtQG9djhIqIu_hUF0XA25D9HcImZ1GTwYiqkjo2Yf--Hsotn6kkDrbyW8a69oEB_6bX4NHzLFVVLzIYBE5mU4Tt1CzHF7X3_fHhDDDPAxiWqs0FycF1Dj2_toc1gOme7ByXLFUtcz3rduu1YnVCAuMKVuxozQFhQHaPWtikrg6ejl1gDNqRjTjf7rHaUk3g==", "published": "2026-07-26", "summary": "As AI continues to automate technical skills like software development, the labor market is entering a \"narrative edge era\" where non-STEM majors (such as English and Social Science graduates) are finding clearer career pathways into the tech sector because of their strong storytelling, persuasion, and branding skills.", "image": "https://imageio.forbes.com/specials-images/imageserve/6a6309a6a90d2729eacafbb7/0x0.jpg?format=jpg&height=900&width=1600&fit=bounds", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=forbes.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "One chart shows why even non-tech job seekers should get comfortable with AI", "source": "Business Insider", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHO3fU5P429pSCtgVGslc1QlyGvLN1c-gjerhQzUCN7O9wrJVnCkVvgjFkrSCgUGylxfdvP6IHyIACKe3051KuHHRlJfU4n9_BIB-CVEwAc9-emkUOacM9QxXFx1FDrIo81lL4oSW8HqdveJNN8BC7DIxNIV63clB7gFK7isp29mdkZrzp7NXm4UNavZyE=", "published": "2026-07-10", "summary": "An analysis of Indeed job postings shows that 63% of \"AI-touched\" US job titles are now in non-tech fields, with sectors like management, marketing, education, and instruction seeing the fastest growth in employers seeking candidates who can pair domain-specific expertise with AI systems.", "image": "https://i.insider.com/6a4f804dd3b3e45765196e0d?width=1200&format=jpeg", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=businessinsider.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "AI Ethics and Digital Humanities Demand", "source": "Research.com", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHKiWHGPGu9shnVQ4DnEui0jNXUNFpOl0tiz9X4jeCu8KOPsl7BCLoUNaQ4gvY2LjjpfYGbiNuJhJNyXjidxC1YB1lpPDseyjAH5gb8G4pJIGkn9gumHtz54F6vYAT8lkuKszhyhou5auJD3Qmy0k1fOVGMlQ6isNr7CsSV4ouFqPbVSluMCgshCDzzgWLSFl8=", "published": "2026-07-16", "summary": "While AI has automated routine copy-editing and entry-level content tasks, it has simultaneously driven a 30% increase in demand for humanities graduates in specialized, interdisciplinary fields like ethical AI development and digital humanities.", "image": null, "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=research.com&sz=64"}]}}, "Trades": {"expires_at": 1785197407.074032, "feed": {"family": "Trades", "fetched_at": "2026-07-27T18:10:07+00:00", "items": [{"title": "Report Highlights Changing Views on Skilled Trades", "source": "Jobber via Business Journal Daily", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFPGHytNLIaKZC9hCIL364ZshKMm-Kb0sah-cIa-Z9E6nAXqSH5U15KaSl0ubfDZvii17gjk7SZ_5c2QfND_lnF9UOgvS6FnVvZdBkpOYCIcmssJM3dIsYYjb1dJcIMgsHxVr0dywwFDAMYAlucgSw75oycD5LeHdkwudJmfA02Uc9JdLtl4nOehBNaEprPMA==", "published": "2026-07-23", "summary": "A comprehensive survey of over 2,000 Gen Z Americans and parents reveals that 68% of parents are rethinking the stability of white-collar careers due to AI, with 38% noting that AI tools make skilled trade careers\u2014which are difficult to automate\u2014far more appealing.", "image": "https://businessjournaldaily.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Electrician-adobe-stock.jpg", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=businessjournaldaily.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "How AI Is Changing Skilled Trades in 2026 (Your Job Is Safer Than You Think)", "source": "The Blue Collar Recruiter", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFnzYsIaIGKXePLuDLLNlKDDRdhjs2MvJUVAWwhvvL2Pe8zNtq7yMh5Ed4Fvkq2g94qViK60kblVBFNC6mQ4rWQbzOyJN2__5DBTK1rAZCbuKp4Nz4I_pb7Gr25I5X7wJs7ES4ccd6vWRGhWms8A9s4uwS0KBdH8RieeUhfCLvhcuXe-oF1lR8pJIa797ATzkMJh2BkGR4FDrWCI-nVqFVWDxMZo9pT-Qu322ZleA==", "published": "2026-06-05", "summary": "This industry report outlines how the AI boom is actively creating hands-on work, as the massive physical infrastructure behind AI\u2014such as data centers and server farms\u2014requires specialized, non-automatable physical labor from electricians, pipefitters, and HVAC technicians to build and cool.", "image": "https://thebluecollarrecruiter.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cropped_e384de7d-8029-4e22-8dfe-a9059568325b_1780414370.jpg", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=thebluecollarrecruiter.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "Skilled Trades Survey 2026: How Gen Z Views AI & College", "source": "SimplyWise", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE6jFKMfDrrS4bqzxjbBbOheScXz1WyIlhY-gQnRny8pESHJIwYtjil4qV4hy2DIv4qEvUjB2JP3GcjQ0gYLl3TBIdKSA2EpZ5ZDuIGwgEPyE_z5pTTCLrtSLIsqkdZJaE9pdVUEDjrjoyVtj0bjGJHpCPdzH6A", "published": "2026-06-02", "summary": "Highlighting a major generational shift, this survey of Gen Z adults found that 52% of current college students believe the skilled trades are safer from AI-driven disruption than traditional office jobs, driving a surge in the social respect and appeal of vocational careers.", "image": "https://www.simplywise.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/skilled-trades-survey-2026-social-card.png", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=simplywise.com&sz=64"}]}}}
